  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMMUNITY ECOGUARDS PROVIDE IMPROVED PROTECTION FOR WESTERN CHIMPANZEES AT KRAHN-BASSA PROPOSED PROTECTED AREA, SOUTHEASTERN LIBERIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO PROTECT THE SECOND LARGEST POPULATION OF ENDANGERED WESTERN CHIMPANZEES IN LIBERIA THROUGH GAZETTEMENT OF THE KRAHN-BASSA PROPOSED PROTECTED AREA (KBPPA) AS LIBERIA S LARGEST NATIONAL PARK BY: (1) INCREASING THE NUMBER OF COMMUNITY ECOMONITORING TEAMS, IMPLEMENTING SMART DATA COLLECTION, AND SHARING OF INFORMATION WITH THE PARK AUTHORITIES (2) INCREASING LOCAL COMMUNITIES AWARENESS OF HUMAN-CHIMP CONFLICT AND HOW TO AVOID IT AND (3) IMPROVING COMMUNITY ECOMONITORING COLLABORATION WITH LIBERIA S WILDLIFE CRIME TASK FORCE THROUGH INCREASED TRAINING, COMMUNICATION, AND JOINT MONITORING ACTIVITIES.</narrative>
  </description>
